          # ⚙️ Data Engineering Pipeline

Data Engineering is the foundation of this project. Instead of directly connecting raw CSV files to Power BI, a structured ETL pipeline was designed to transform raw transactional datasets into business-ready analytical data.

The pipeline focuses on data quality, consistency, scalability, and performance while following industry-standard Data Engineering practices.

---

# 🎯 Data Engineering Objectives

The primary objectives of the Data Engineering layer were:

- Automate data ingestion
- Standardize raw datasets
- Improve data quality
- Validate business data
- Build reusable SQL transformations
- Create an analytical data warehouse
- Support scalable reporting
- Enable downstream Business Intelligence

---

# 🏗 Data Engineering Workflow

```text
              Raw CSV Files
                     │
                     ▼
          Python ETL Pipeline
                     │
                     ▼
         MySQL Relational Database
                     │
                     ▼
        SQL Data Cleaning Layer
                     │
                     ▼
      SQL Business Transformations
                     │
                     ▼
         Data Validation Layer
                     │
                     ▼
        Dimensional Data Warehouse
                     │
                     ▼
      SQL Analytics & Business Views
                     │
                     ▼
             Power BI Dashboards
```

---

# 📥 Extract Layer

The project begins by extracting multiple retail datasets stored in CSV format.

The source datasets include:

- Customer Information
- Product Information
- Sales Transactions
- Market Information
- Gross Price
- Manufacturing Cost
- Freight Cost
- Pre-Invoice Deductions
- Post-Invoice Deductions
- Operational Expenses
- Monthly Sales Forecast

Each dataset represents a different business entity and is loaded independently before transformation.

---

# 🐍 Python ETL Pipeline

Python was used to automate the Extract and Load phases of the pipeline.

## Responsibilities

- Reading raw CSV files
- Data type conversion
- Column standardization
- Bulk loading into MySQL
- Exception handling
- Logging ETL execution
- Basic preprocessing

## ETL Features

- Automated Data Loading
- CSV Processing
- Database Connectivity
- Batch Insert Operations
- Data Validation
- Error Handling
- Logging
- Reusable Python Scripts

---

# 🗄 Database Layer

MySQL serves as the central data repository for the entire analytics solution.

Instead of performing business calculations inside Power BI, all business-ready datasets are prepared inside the database.

## Database Responsibilities

- Centralized Storage
- Data Integrity
- Relationship Management
- SQL Processing
- Business Logic Execution
- High-performance Querying

---

# 🧹 SQL Data Cleaning

Once the raw datasets are loaded, SQL is used to clean and standardize the data before analysis.

Cleaning activities include:

- NULL Value Handling
- Duplicate Detection
- Data Type Standardization
- Invalid Record Identification
- Missing Value Handling
- Data Consistency Checks
- Business Rule Validation

---

# 🔄 SQL Data Transformation

Business-ready datasets are created through SQL transformations.

Transformations include:

- CASE WHEN Logic
- COALESCE()
- IFNULL()
- UPDATE Statements
- Derived Columns
- Business Calculations
- Lookup Integration

These transformations convert raw transactional data into structured analytical datasets.

---

# 🏛 Data Warehouse Design

A dimensional data warehouse was designed using the Star Schema approach.

The warehouse separates transactional facts from descriptive dimensions to simplify reporting and improve query performance.

## Fact Tables

- fact_sales_monthly
- fact_forecast_monthly
- helper_ clean(fact_actual_estimate)

## Dimension Tables

- dim_customer
- dim_product
- dim_market
- dim_date

## Supporting Business Tables

- gross_price
- manufacturing_cost
- freight_cost
- pre_invoice_deductions
- post_invoice_deductions
- operational_expenses
- market_sales 

---

# ⭐ Star Schema

The analytical model follows a Star Schema architecture.

```text
                 dim_customer
                      │
                      │
dim_market ─── fact_sales_monthly ─── dim_product
                      │
                      │
                  dim_date

          Supporting Business Tables

Gross Price
Manufacturing Cost
Freight Cost
Invoice Deductions
Operational Expenses
Forecast
```

### Benefits

- Faster Query Performance
- Simplified Data Model
- Reduced Data Redundancy
- Better Scalability
- Easier Power BI Integration

---

# 📅 Custom Date Dimension

Instead of depending on the source dataset, a custom Date Dimension was created using SQL.

The Date Dimension includes:

- Calendar Date
- Calendar Month
- Calendar Quarter
- Calendar Year
- Fiscal Month
- Fiscal Quarter
- Fiscal Year
- Week Number
- Month Name
- Quarter Name

This enables advanced DAX Time Intelligence calculations.

---

# 🔗 Data Relationships

Relationships were designed using business keys to maintain referential integrity.

Examples include:

- Customer → Sales
- Product → Sales
- Market → Sales
- Date → Sales
- Product → Gross Price
- Product → Manufacturing Cost
- Customer → Invoice Deductions
- Forecast → Sales

---

# ✅ Data Validation

To improve reliability, multiple validation checks were performed.

Validation includes:

- NULL Validation
- Duplicate Validation
- Referential Integrity Validation
- Missing Customer Validation
- Missing Product Validation
- Missing Date Validation
- Invalid Data Type Validation

---

# 🔍 Data Profiling

Data profiling was performed before analytical reporting.

Profiling includes:

- Row Count Validation
- Distinct Value Analysis
- Missing Value Analysis
- Data Type Verification
- Distribution Analysis
- Outlier Detection
- Data Completeness Check

---

# ⚡ Database Optimization

Performance optimization techniques were applied to improve SQL execution.

Optimization includes:

- Index Creation
- Optimized JOIN Strategy
- Query Optimization
- Execution Plan Review *(where applicable)*
- Efficient Filtering
- Reduced Query Complexity

---

# 🎯 Engineering Best Practices

The project follows several engineering best practices:

- Modular SQL Scripts
- Layered Architecture
- Reusable SQL Components
- Consistent Naming Conventions
- Star Schema Modeling
- SQL-First Business Logic
- Separation of Transformation and Reporting
- Clean Repository Structure

