          # 📊 Business Intelligence & Power BI

The Business Intelligence layer transforms the enterprise data warehouse into an interactive analytics platform that enables stakeholders to monitor business performance, identify trends, and support strategic decision-making.

Instead of directly importing raw datasets into Power BI, this project connects Power BI to a business-ready SQL data warehouse, ensuring that reports are built on validated, standardized, and optimized data.

---

# 🎯 Business Intelligence Objectives

The primary objectives of the BI layer were to:

- Deliver executive-level dashboards
- Build reusable KPI measures
- Implement advanced DAX calculations
- Enable interactive business exploration
- Support time-based trend analysis
- Improve reporting efficiency
- Provide actionable business insights

---

# 🏗 Power BI Architecture

```text
          SQL Data Warehouse
                  │
                  ▼
         Power Query (ETL)
                  │
                  ▼
      Power BI Semantic Model
                  │
                  ▼
          DAX Calculations
                  │
                  ▼
        Interactive Dashboards
                  │
                  ▼
      Executive Decision Support
```

---

# 🔄 Power Query Transformation

Power Query was used to prepare SQL data for reporting.

### Key Transformations

- Data Type Conversion
- Column Renaming
- Data Formatting
- Relationship Preparation
- Null Value Verification
- Data Consistency Checks

The majority of business transformations were intentionally completed in SQL to keep Power BI lightweight and improve refresh performance.

---

# 🧩 Semantic Data Model

A centralized semantic model was created to establish relationships between fact and dimension tables.

### Fact Tables

- Sales
- Forecast

### Dimension Tables

- Customer
- Product
- Market
- Date

### Benefits

- Single Source of Truth
- Reduced Data Redundancy
- Better DAX Performance
- Consistent KPI Definitions
- Simplified Dashboard Development

---

# 📅 Date Dimension & Time Intelligence

A custom SQL-generated Date Dimension powers all time-based reporting.

### Calendar Attributes

- Date
- Month
- Quarter
- Year
- Week Number

### Fiscal Attributes

- Fiscal Month
- Fiscal Quarter
- Fiscal Year

This enables accurate Time Intelligence calculations across all dashboards.

